      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e `ccuser` can be `None` in the live call paths: `instack.py` passes\n\u003e `assignment.ccuser`, which is `None` when the cloud has no active assignment,\n\u003e and the `ccuser` column is a pickle list that can hold `NULL` for existing\n\u003e rows. Without the guard `for entry in None` raises `TypeError`; the `or []`\n\u003e normalizes that to an empty iteration. (The `isinstance(ccuser, str)` branch\n\u003e just above is defensive for callers that pass a bare string; the summary path\n\u003e already normalizes via `cloud.get(\"ccuser\") or []`.) The falsy / `None` cases\n\u003e are covered by `test_non_string_and_falsy_ccuser_safe` in\n\u003e tests/web/test_auth_helpers.py.",
