      "writtenOn": "2026-09-01T07:39:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Agreed the header parsing overlaps with `check_access()`, but that decorator\n\u003e cannot gate this route as-is:\n\u003e\n\u003e - It lives in the server app and resolves users through `db.session`,\n\u003e   `User.decode_auth_token()` and `ApiTokenDao` - direct database access. The\n\u003e   web frontend has no database bound (`db.session` is never initialized in\n\u003e   that process); it speaks to the API over HTTP as a service account.\n\u003e - It requires an `Authorization` header and returns 400 when one is absent,\n\u003e   while this route must also serve Flask-Login cookie sessions (no header).\n\u003e - Its authorization model is role membership (403 unless the user holds one\n\u003e   of the listed roles); this gate is per-cloud ownership (owner / cc-user /\n\u003e   admin) enforced after identity resolution.\n\u003e\n\u003e The token-to-identity step is already delegated to the server: the new\n\u003e `GET /api/v3/me` endpoint is decorated with `@check_access([\"admin\", \"user\"])`,\n\u003e and `QuadsApi.get_authenticated_user()` forwards the caller\u0027s own bearer\n\u003e token - and only that token; the service-account Basic auth is explicitly\n\u003e bypassed for this call so `/me` cannot resolve to the app\u0027s service account.\n\u003e So `check_access` is reused exactly where database access exists.",
      "parentUuid": "43cf119e_14714a4e",
      "revId": "803791fa2bcbe79b47c7ca3176e6dda320e87612",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
